# A second line of defense, not the first: `deploy/judge/Dockerfile` names every
# path it copies, so nothing arrives by being forgotten here. This narrows the
# build context — and refuses to send anything holding real data even if a COPY
# were widened by accident.

.git
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.next
apps/web/out

# Never. The brain is the subject's memory, `data/` holds payload files — the
# raw, unredacted content `model_call_payloads` points at — and a database here
# would be a real one.
data
brain
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
